WEBVTT

00:02.560 --> 00:05.530
In matters relating
to the world of the dead

00:05.630 --> 00:08.990
there is an institution that judges
the sins of the deceased

00:09.250 --> 00:10.790
the Ju-Oh-Cho.

00:11.630 --> 00:13.400
The Summons Section
of the Judgment Bureau

00:13.500 --> 00:17.230
comprises a group supporting
the ministry's operating functions

00:17.340 --> 00:20.170
by guiding the lost souls
that wander the mortal world.

00:20.540 --> 00:22.170
They are also known as...

00:22.410 --> 00:24.850
the Shinigami.

00:25.110 --> 00:31.780
nureta hitomi no oku

00:25.110 --> 00:31.780
Deep behind its wavering stare

00:33.490 --> 00:43.800
aoi tsuki wa shizuka ni koboreochiteyuku

00:33.490 --> 00:43.800
The pale moon quietly descends

00:33.570 --> 00:42.820
Yami no Matsuei

00:50.110 --> 00:55.980
azayaka na sekai wa

00:50.110 --> 00:55.980
The splendid world

00:58.350 --> 01:08.420
oto mo naku shizuka ni yami ni kieteyuku

00:58.350 --> 01:08.420
Disappears into the darkness without a sound

01:08.520 --> 01:16.160
byouyomi no naka kakemeguru yami no naka o

01:08.520 --> 01:16.160
Running about in the dark as time runs out

01:16.260 --> 01:22.790
soshite aratanaru toki o mukae ima

01:16.260 --> 01:22.790
A new era beckons now

01:25.510 --> 01:30.600
kizutsuita kuroi tsubasa

01:25.510 --> 01:30.600
The injured black wings

01:30.780 --> 01:37.150
tsuki no akari ni terasarete

01:30.780 --> 01:37.150
Shine in the moonlight

01:37.750 --> 01:41.950
utsukushiku maiagare

01:37.750 --> 01:41.950
Rising upward in a beautiful dance

01:42.090 --> 01:47.290
shinku no kuchizuke ga ima

01:42.090 --> 01:47.290
The crimson kiss

01:47.400 --> 01:54.230
kokoro no oku ni nagarekomu

01:47.400 --> 01:54.230
Flows deeply into the soul

01:54.400 --> 02:00.200
soshite yume no naka e

01:54.400 --> 02:00.200
Penetrating into one's dreams

02:11.840 --> 02:13.630
Wonderful...

02:13.740 --> 02:17.200
I will now be among the top violinists.

02:17.310 --> 02:21.110
With this violin, there is nothing I have to fear.

02:32.310 --> 02:37.320
Episode 4: Devil's Trill, Part 1

02:40.070 --> 02:42.070
Ophthalmologist Examination Room

02:42.030 --> 02:45.030
Now slowly open your eyes.

02:47.910 --> 02:49.370
Well? Can you see my hand?

02:49.480 --> 02:50.600
Y-Yes.

02:50.710 --> 02:51.870
Good.

02:51.980 --> 02:54.340
Now I want you to look out the window.

02:54.580 --> 02:56.510
Can you see far as well?

03:06.560 --> 03:07.920
Uh, what?

03:08.030 --> 03:09.290
Huh? Does it hurt?

03:09.390 --> 03:11.060
Uh, no.

03:11.730 --> 03:13.460
But what a relief.

03:13.570 --> 03:16.160
This means I can play the violin again.

03:16.670 --> 03:20.540
You were lucky there was a cornea donor.

03:21.310 --> 03:23.670
Well, let's get you discharged.

03:23.780 --> 03:25.770
Uh, could you hang on a second?

03:25.880 --> 03:30.180
I'd like to thank the person
who donated his cornea.

03:30.380 --> 03:31.850
You want to thank the donor?

03:31.950 --> 03:33.540
That won't be possible.

03:33.650 --> 03:36.350
Otonashi-san, the donor,
has already passed away.

03:36.990 --> 03:38.920
Then what about his family?

03:39.020 --> 03:42.720
I don't feel right about
not giving them my thanks.

03:43.760 --> 03:45.060
Family, huh?

03:46.030 --> 03:50.470
I believe Otonashi-san had
a daughter called Kazusa.

03:50.740 --> 03:53.570
I hear she's the only family.

03:53.670 --> 03:56.570
So she's an orphan just like you.

04:00.780 --> 04:02.770
Kazusa-san, you have a guest.

04:02.880 --> 04:04.680
Okay!

04:06.720 --> 04:08.880
Who are you?

04:14.430 --> 04:18.090
Um, I'm Minase Hijiri.

04:18.200 --> 04:21.560
If you're Hijiri, can I call you Hi-chan?

04:22.300 --> 04:26.070
Uh, sure. I'm here to thank you.

04:26.540 --> 04:27.600
Thank me?

04:27.710 --> 04:31.370
Because your father
donated his cornea...

04:31.480 --> 04:35.280
I'm able to see now. That's why.

04:36.520 --> 04:38.420
I'm glad for you, Hi-chan.

04:38.520 --> 04:40.310
I also want to apologize.

04:40.420 --> 04:42.550
Why do you apologize?

04:44.260 --> 04:47.380
I'm fine. I really am.

04:47.490 --> 04:49.290
I'm fine.

04:49.730 --> 04:50.990
Kazusa...

04:53.430 --> 04:54.800
Is that your violin?

04:54.900 --> 04:57.370
Uh, yeah. That's right.

04:57.470 --> 05:00.440
My father used to play violin too.

05:00.540 --> 05:03.130
- He was really good at it.
- Is that right?

05:03.410 --> 05:07.850
Promise me that I'll one day
be able to hear you play?

05:08.480 --> 05:09.710
Promise?

05:09.820 --> 05:11.580
Sure. It's a promise.

05:12.820 --> 05:14.380
Pledge to make a promise...

05:14.490 --> 05:18.650
and if you lie, you'll have to drink poison!

05:26.000 --> 05:29.660
<i>I've been in a state of despair since then.</i>

05:30.540 --> 05:33.400
<i>My chest feels tight, and
it's sometimes hard to breathe.</i>

05:33.910 --> 05:37.810
<i>I feel as though I killed Kazusa's father.</i>

05:40.450 --> 05:41.910
<i>That night...</i>

05:42.010 --> 05:46.850
<i>I felt guilty about my own
existence for the first time.</i>

05:52.310 --> 05:54.180
Principal's Office

05:52.660 --> 05:56.090
Well, I'm so glad that
you're feeling much better.

05:56.330 --> 05:58.130
Thank you.

05:58.230 --> 05:59.860
There's one thing.

05:59.970 --> 06:03.160
Our regular concert series is
coming up next week, right?

06:03.700 --> 06:08.330
I want you to perform
a solo violin piece.

06:09.740 --> 06:12.800
I'll leave you to decide
what music to play.

06:13.280 --> 06:14.510
Don't worry.

06:14.610 --> 06:17.980
I'm sure you'll have no problem
getting right back into it.

06:18.080 --> 06:19.850
I'm looking forward to it, Minase-kun.

06:19.950 --> 06:22.440
Yes. Thank you.

06:22.750 --> 06:24.310
Hijiri!

06:24.420 --> 06:26.580
It's been such a long time!

06:26.690 --> 06:28.250
Your eyes are okay now?

06:28.560 --> 06:30.390
Can't you tell?

06:30.630 --> 06:32.430
Thank goodness!

06:32.530 --> 06:36.930
We've all been waiting for you
to come back to school.

06:37.140 --> 06:42.230
Things were pretty crazy around
school while you were away.

06:42.340 --> 06:46.540
Ordinary people like us have been
pushed aside into a corner.

06:46.850 --> 06:50.940
A violin solo concert
by Minase Hijiri-kun, huh?

06:51.050 --> 06:54.820
Good work promoting yourself
after your absence.

06:54.920 --> 06:55.910
Saionji...

06:56.320 --> 06:58.450
Is this some kind of joke?

06:58.560 --> 07:00.720
The idiot principal.

07:00.830 --> 07:03.920
He ignores the students who have
been practicing diligently

07:04.030 --> 07:07.430
in favor of letting some guy
who was practically dead

07:07.530 --> 07:08.730
to do the solo concert.

07:08.830 --> 07:11.200
What are you trying to say?

07:11.800 --> 07:15.000
We're saying that if you weren't
such a pet of the principal's

07:15.110 --> 07:17.080
you wouldn't have been given that job.

07:17.180 --> 07:18.700
Watch that attitude of yours.

07:18.810 --> 07:22.110
I don't care if you're
the All-Japan winner.

07:22.210 --> 07:25.050
If you carry on the way you've
been, you might get hurt.

07:25.150 --> 07:27.710
- All right, Minase?
- Stupid idiot.

07:27.820 --> 07:30.550
You incompetent rich boys
ought to stay out of this.

07:30.660 --> 07:31.620
What'd you say?!

07:31.720 --> 07:34.020
Wait until you beat me at least once

07:34.130 --> 07:36.860
before you go spouting off like that, Saionji.

07:36.960 --> 07:39.190
Whether it be violin or fist fighting

07:39.300 --> 07:41.270
you'll never be a match for me.

07:41.370 --> 07:42.700
Well...

07:42.800 --> 07:47.430
for a rich boy whose daddy's
money got him a place here

07:47.540 --> 07:50.870
I'd say a million years
wouldn't be enough.

07:52.440 --> 07:54.280
Don't you forget this, Minase!

07:54.380 --> 07:57.970
I'll show you what happens
when you come against me.

07:58.980 --> 08:01.210
Go on! Run away!

08:06.530 --> 08:07.490
Are you okay?!

08:07.590 --> 08:09.120
Hijiri!

08:12.280 --> 08:15.030
Infirmary Room

08:13.170 --> 08:14.760
Excuse me.

08:21.370 --> 08:22.570
What's the matter?

08:22.670 --> 08:25.670
Uh, huh?
Where's the doctor?

08:25.780 --> 08:29.240
Oh, Dr. Hara's sick, so he took the day off.

08:29.350 --> 08:30.970
I'm the substitute.

08:31.280 --> 08:34.980
Well, can I get some painkillers?
I have a headache.

08:35.090 --> 08:36.490
Sure.

08:36.590 --> 08:38.420
Let's see.

08:38.860 --> 08:40.980
Here. Have some of
this herbal medicine.

08:41.090 --> 08:42.680
That's for the stomach.

08:43.030 --> 08:45.260
Good grief.

08:48.000 --> 08:50.430
Get it together, Doc.

08:52.270 --> 08:54.430
I'll be more careful next time.

08:54.640 --> 08:55.770
Here.

08:58.880 --> 09:01.850
The resemblance is uncanny.

09:03.660 --> 09:05.710
Music Room Nº1

09:11.210 --> 09:14.170
Shomiwa School of Music
Minase Hijiri

09:20.560 --> 09:23.020
Fire Alarm

09:23.500 --> 09:25.970
- Hey, what's going on?!
- I-It's a fire!

09:26.070 --> 09:27.700
Wh-Where's it from?!

09:27.810 --> 09:29.210
The Music Room Nº1!

09:30.080 --> 09:32.170
Our violins!

09:47.460 --> 09:52.000
Yami no Matsuei

09:53.870 --> 09:55.460
I'm sorry, Kazusa.

09:56.800 --> 10:00.130
I don't think I can keep
that promise I made.

10:00.240 --> 10:01.430
Why?

10:02.370 --> 10:07.400
There was a fire at my school,
and my violin was burned.

10:08.350 --> 10:11.250
That was a memento
from my dead father.

10:11.350 --> 10:15.620
It was a cheap, old violin that
always sounded out of tune.

10:16.150 --> 10:19.680
But it was the one thing that
was able to understand me.

10:19.790 --> 10:21.780
It was like an extension of my body.

10:26.630 --> 10:27.930
Kazusa?

10:29.630 --> 10:31.760
I'll give this to you, Hi-chan.

10:34.170 --> 10:35.900
You know, Kazusa...

10:36.010 --> 10:39.070
each and every violin is a little different.

10:39.180 --> 10:42.270
The person playing it
has to be in tune with it

10:42.380 --> 10:44.410
or you can't produce a beautiful sound.

10:44.520 --> 10:46.950
You can't just substitute violins.

10:49.990 --> 10:52.680
This is the violin that my father used.

10:52.790 --> 10:55.260
It's my precious treasure.

10:55.360 --> 10:58.120
But I want you to feel better
and become well, so...

11:03.300 --> 11:05.130
<i>Incredible!</i>

11:05.240 --> 11:07.330
<i>I feel like its sucking in my soul.</i>

11:08.410 --> 11:10.070
Are you sure I can have this?

11:10.180 --> 11:11.370
Sure.

11:11.480 --> 11:15.670
I think even the violin would
be happy if you played it.

11:21.010 --> 11:22.990
Music Room Nº5

11:22.990 --> 11:24.920
That's wrong, Yamashita!

11:25.320 --> 11:28.050
Look carefully.
It's a double flat there!

11:28.160 --> 11:29.420
I-I'm sorry.

11:29.690 --> 11:32.720
If you can't play music as simple as this

11:32.830 --> 11:35.730
I can't have you play in the concert series.

11:35.830 --> 11:37.530
That's enough.
Get back to your seat.

11:37.670 --> 11:40.400
- Yes, sir.
- I know, sir.

11:40.810 --> 11:44.240
How about we have Minase-kun show us his stuff?

11:44.340 --> 11:46.110
I agree! I agree!

11:46.710 --> 11:49.370
He is a genius after all.

11:49.480 --> 11:53.210
He should be able to get used
to a new violin pretty quickly.

11:53.590 --> 11:55.050
I-I wonder...

11:55.790 --> 11:57.550
All right then.
Minase, you're next.

11:57.660 --> 11:59.020
Y-Yes, sir.

12:14.940 --> 12:16.870
Amazing!

12:22.610 --> 12:24.780
Th-The Devil's Trill.

12:25.350 --> 12:28.380
When did he master that difficult piece?!

12:29.050 --> 12:31.420
Hijiri must be a genius after all.

12:37.660 --> 12:39.630
That's enough, Minase!

12:42.970 --> 12:44.800
Wh-What's up with him?!

12:45.140 --> 12:46.570
He looks crazed!

12:46.670 --> 12:48.370
And look at his eye!

12:57.950 --> 12:59.140
The devil?

12:59.250 --> 13:02.010
What I'm trying to say is
that he was playing

13:02.120 --> 13:04.420
a piece called ''The Devil's Trill.''

13:04.520 --> 13:08.050
Now there's a rumor that
he's been possessed by the devil.

13:08.160 --> 13:12.060
The whole school's in a panic over this.

13:12.160 --> 13:14.890
By the way, what's this ''Devil's Trill''?

13:15.000 --> 13:16.090
Don't you know?

13:16.200 --> 13:21.330
It's a violin sonata composed by the
Italian composer Guiseppe Tartini.

13:21.440 --> 13:25.270
They say he wrote it after
selling his soul to the devil

13:25.380 --> 13:27.280
and making a pact with the devil.

13:27.480 --> 13:30.780
It's one of the most difficult
pieces of violin music to play.

13:31.280 --> 13:34.910
They say that even a pro
has a hard time playing it.

13:35.020 --> 13:37.850
Even if you've been marked by the devil.

13:40.990 --> 13:42.690
The Devil's Trill, huh?

13:53.340 --> 13:55.240
<i>There's Minase.</i>

13:55.670 --> 13:57.940
<i>Do you think those rumors are true?</i>

13:58.040 --> 14:01.140
<i>He kept playing the Devil's Trill
even though he was bleeding?</i>

14:01.250 --> 14:04.580
<i>His left eye shines in gold color at night!</i>

14:04.980 --> 14:08.080
<i>A genius is one step away
from becoming a monster.</i>

14:09.820 --> 14:11.350
Now be careful.

14:14.360 --> 14:15.720
Kazusa.

14:17.600 --> 14:18.930
Don't come near me!

14:19.030 --> 14:21.430
Now, now.
What's going on, Kazusa?

14:22.130 --> 14:24.290
It's just Mr. Minase.

14:41.690 --> 14:43.620
- You're the devil!
- What're you doing?!

14:43.720 --> 14:44.950
I'm scared!

14:45.060 --> 14:46.280
Don't look at me!

14:46.390 --> 14:49.220
You're not the Hijiri that I know!
You're the devil!

14:49.660 --> 14:50.890
N-No!

14:54.230 --> 14:56.030
Where's my father?

14:56.130 --> 14:58.730
Please! I want my father back!

14:59.170 --> 15:00.640
I want him back!

15:03.910 --> 15:05.930
Minase Hijiri.

15:06.040 --> 15:09.410
Your existence itself is
the source of your guilt.

15:11.950 --> 15:15.410
You have no worth and no reason to live.

15:15.520 --> 15:18.150
That's right.
That's totally right.

15:18.890 --> 15:21.980
I should've done this much sooner.

15:23.630 --> 15:27.360
On the night when I felt guilty
about my own existence.

15:45.580 --> 15:47.050
Where am I?

15:48.090 --> 15:51.150
Why would there be cherry
blossoms at this time of year?

15:52.160 --> 15:53.750
Am I in heaven?

15:53.860 --> 15:57.020
Unfortunately, this is not heaven.

15:57.960 --> 15:59.830
But it's not hell either.

15:59.930 --> 16:02.870
Welcome to the Judgment Bureau, Minase Hijiri.

16:03.070 --> 16:06.330
Y-You're the substitute
from the infirmary!

16:06.440 --> 16:07.530
And you're--

16:14.110 --> 16:16.410
Who on earth are you guys, anyway?

16:16.880 --> 16:18.470
We're not human beings.

16:18.580 --> 16:21.950
We work for the Summons Section
of the Judgment Bureau.

16:22.050 --> 16:24.150
- We're Shinigami.
- Shinigami?!

16:24.990 --> 16:27.290
Th-Then does that mean I'm dead?

16:27.390 --> 16:31.760
No, you're not dead.
But you did sustain a severe injury.

16:31.860 --> 16:36.530
You have a violin, don't you?
A gift from Otonashi Kazusa?

16:36.630 --> 16:39.230
Yeah, but what does that
have to do with anything?

16:40.740 --> 16:42.470
There's quite a story to it.

16:43.240 --> 16:45.510
It produces a beautiful sound when you play it.

16:45.610 --> 16:49.510
One that will improve the
violinist's skill several fold.

16:50.350 --> 16:55.310
But it belongs to the devil who
will suck your soul out in exchange.

16:55.420 --> 16:57.290
Wh-What is this nonsense?

16:57.390 --> 16:58.980
This isn't some cartoon.

16:59.360 --> 17:03.260
And it will torment the owner
of the violin psychologically

17:03.360 --> 17:05.060
driving him to commit suicide.

17:05.160 --> 17:08.190
Just like how you cut your
throat open in that chapel.

17:15.840 --> 17:19.570
Apparently hundreds have died
from it in other countries.

17:19.680 --> 17:23.610
And now it's come to Japan.
What a panic!

17:24.050 --> 17:27.020
As we were tracking down the violin

17:27.120 --> 17:31.320
we came across a man called Otonashi Tatsuya.

17:32.190 --> 17:35.630
But he'd already died accidentally
before we caught up to him.

17:35.730 --> 17:39.630
We had no choice but to ask
his daughter Kazusa about it

17:39.730 --> 17:42.790
but she wouldn't say
anything about the violin.

17:44.940 --> 17:48.600
We pleaded with the nun
to get a hold of this instead.

17:48.710 --> 17:51.140
This is Otonashi's diary.

17:51.240 --> 17:52.710
We should have been able to learn

17:52.810 --> 17:56.440
how he got that violin
from what's written here.

17:56.550 --> 17:59.310
And from investigating the diary

17:59.420 --> 18:02.410
we weren't able to figure out
the origin of the violin,

18:02.520 --> 18:04.820
but something unbelievable
was written in there.

18:04.920 --> 18:06.050
Gushoushin.

18:06.160 --> 18:07.220
Right!

18:07.990 --> 18:10.550
I had a strange dream last night.

18:10.660 --> 18:15.120
<i>An enormous devil with black wings
appeared in my dream.</i>

18:15.500 --> 18:18.560
<i>And he offered to grant me
my most cherished wish</i>

18:18.670 --> 18:21.300
<i>in exchange for my most
dearest possession.</i>

18:22.070 --> 18:25.470
<i>Well, I figured that this was only a dream</i>

18:25.580 --> 18:30.570
<i>so I asked the devil to make me
into a successful violinist,</i>

18:30.680 --> 18:34.080
<i>and to give my daughter
status and position in life</i>

18:34.190 --> 18:35.980
<i>such that she can live comfortably.</i>

18:36.190 --> 18:39.380
<i>That's when the devil
touched my left eye</i>

18:39.490 --> 18:41.010
<i>and said as he laughed...</i>

18:41.130 --> 18:43.560
<i>''Don't you forget. This is the contract.''</i>

18:48.700 --> 18:53.640
<i>In the next moment, a terrible burn
and light assaulted my left eye.</i>

18:53.740 --> 18:56.040
<i>It was the seal of the contract.</i>

18:59.140 --> 19:00.370
No way!

19:01.250 --> 19:06.110
The cornea that was transplanted
to your left eye, Hijiri.

19:07.690 --> 19:11.990
Not only that, you also possess that violin.

19:12.090 --> 19:14.790
A cursed violin and a contract with the devil.

19:14.890 --> 19:16.760
Seems too much, don't you think?

19:20.630 --> 19:22.790
Here's what we'll do, Hijiri.

19:23.070 --> 19:25.930
I want to do some tests on your left eye.

19:26.040 --> 19:30.630
We need to find out what sort of
pact Otonashi made with the devil.

19:30.910 --> 19:34.070
But I don't know.

19:34.250 --> 19:36.150
Don't you worry, Hijiri.

19:37.520 --> 19:40.580
You can be sure that we will protect you.

19:40.690 --> 19:43.180
We won't let you get hurt.

19:44.190 --> 19:45.820
You'll have to trust us.

19:49.490 --> 19:50.460
All right.

19:56.230 --> 19:58.830
There's a small scratch on the cornea.

19:58.940 --> 20:00.430
This is probably the contract.

20:00.940 --> 20:02.300
What the heck is that?

20:02.410 --> 20:06.000
It's coded, so that it can't be read.

20:06.110 --> 20:08.870
It's what they call an anagram.

20:08.980 --> 20:10.450
He's pretty good, that devil.

20:10.550 --> 20:13.070
Don't flatter him. Just decode it.

20:13.180 --> 20:14.520
Yes, yes.

20:17.260 --> 20:19.660
Huh? Wh-What is this?

20:19.760 --> 20:21.730
All right. I'll read it.

20:22.090 --> 20:24.460
The one who has entered into this contract

20:24.560 --> 20:28.460
shall gain stature as a violinist
under the mark of the devil.

20:28.570 --> 20:31.730
In exchange, when the
contractor's goal is attained

20:31.840 --> 20:36.030
he shall hand over the life
of his daughter to me.

20:36.140 --> 20:39.200
By daughter, does he mean Kazusa?!

20:39.310 --> 20:40.570
What does this mean?!

20:40.680 --> 20:43.550
Well, I can't really answer that.

20:43.650 --> 20:47.140
Normally this contract
would have been fulfilled

20:47.250 --> 20:50.020
when Otonashi Tatsuya died accidentally.

20:50.120 --> 20:53.680
However, because his cornea
which serves as the contract

20:53.790 --> 20:55.590
was transplanted into Hijiri,

20:55.690 --> 20:59.360
Otonashi Tatsuya has, in a
strange sense, continued to live.

20:59.730 --> 21:00.990
I see.

21:01.100 --> 21:05.870
As long as even one cell of the
contractor lives, the contract lives.

21:05.970 --> 21:11.640
In other words, this devil will
have to fulfill the contract again.

21:11.980 --> 21:16.850
The devil wouldn't accept
anything less reasonable.

21:17.210 --> 21:18.410
That's right.

21:18.520 --> 21:20.810
Hijiri's life is actually in danger.

21:20.920 --> 21:22.980
He was even induced to commit suicide.

21:23.090 --> 21:25.920
The devil wants to kill Hijiri

21:26.020 --> 21:29.790
and eliminate Otonashi Tatsuya,
who continues to live within Hijiri.

21:29.890 --> 21:33.090
Then the contract will be fulfilled.

21:39.960 --> 21:42.960
Next Episode

21:42.870 --> 21:44.740
In Minase Hijiri's left cornea

21:44.840 --> 21:47.440
there was a contract seal with the devil.

21:47.550 --> 21:49.880
Just leave it to me, Tsuzuki.

21:49.980 --> 21:53.280
I, Watari-sama, will reveal its identity.

21:53.380 --> 21:56.110
It'll be a piece of cake!

21:56.220 --> 21:58.150
You mean with a Ouija board?!

21:59.920 --> 22:04.360
Next time on Yami no Matsuei: The Devil's Trill, Part 2

22:00.060 --> 22:09.970
Episode 5          Devil's Trill, Part 2

22:04.800 --> 22:07.960
Those who live in the darkness wander aimlessly.

22:18.230 --> 22:21.590
arumikan no marui en o mashikaku ni orinagara

22:18.230 --> 22:21.590
As I square the round edges on the drink

22:21.700 --> 22:24.630
kimi o matsu machikado sa

22:21.700 --> 22:24.630
I wait for you on the street corner

22:24.730 --> 22:28.220
nakami no ekitai wa mou nurukute nomenai kedo

22:24.730 --> 22:28.220
The liquid inside is warm and I can't drink it anymore

22:28.340 --> 22:30.930
shikatanaku motsu ore sa

22:28.340 --> 22:30.930
But what can I do but hold onto to it?

22:31.040 --> 22:38.270
yami no naka de ore o utsusu
garasu keesu ni kazarareta

22:31.040 --> 22:38.270
In the glass case reflecting me in the darkness

22:38.380 --> 22:45.010
ningyou ga sakki kara kowai
kao de ore o miteru

22:38.380 --> 22:45.010
There is a doll that has been scowling at me

22:58.470 --> 23:04.890
ore no fuku kuchibue wa wari
to akarui uta de

22:58.470 --> 23:04.890
The tune I whistle is a bright and cheerful one

23:05.410 --> 23:11.340
zensekai no hitotachi ni
sasagerareta noizu

23:05.410 --> 23:11.340
A little noise dedicated to the people of the world

23:12.110 --> 23:18.450
dare hitori shiru hazu
no nai kono merodi ga

23:12.110 --> 23:18.450
No one could possibly recognize the melody

23:19.200 --> 23:24.600
omae ni wa kikoeru ka? Sayonara da
Love me

23:19.200 --> 23:24.600
But do you hear it?
Good-bye, Love me
